# Official-client account lifecycle and strict HTTP integration patch.
# Target: rustdesk/rustdesk 092a961b629d318fe290eeafac0cd214a1e9deeb.
# Apply from the pinned client's flutter/ directory with git apply.
# Only the six listed official Dart files and a new Dart lifecycle helper are
# involved. No application copy, generated binding, manifest, runner or media
# path is part of this patch. The existing official login/verification/OIDC,
# legacy/shared address-book CRUD and group pagination remain Dart-owned.
#
# Integration adaptations (not claimed to be an upstream transplant):
# - Captured API/token/generation and rendezvous/key trust context; checked
#   result unwrapping in the resumed consumer closes the Future microtask gap.
# - One bounded account-native-write/transition queue; native start/poll and
#   already-submitted option/cache writes drain before revocation/replacement.
# - Password/OIDC/verification UI publishes login only after protected commit.
#   Logout captures the old endpoint/headers and resets inside the same queue,
#   before server options are changed. A later login cannot be cleared by it.
# - Per-model cache revision fences retire old saves without logging out.
#   Ab cache deserialize resets only model state, not credentials or disk cache.
# - Both HTTP branches require HTTPS and reject redirects; pure Dart uses the
#   existing http Client without a certificate override. Native transport must
#   also enforce trust/redirect policy; this patch is not its substitute.
# - Exceptions/response bodies/authBody/userInfo/headers/query URLs are not
#   emitted in diagnostics. Authorised business response data is not stripped.
#
# Native integration prerequisites: the fixed fallible account local-option,
# HTTP/OIDC and protected cache implementations, with paired generated bindings.
# No additional Dart dependency or public FRB method/request ID is introduced.
# Native and optional non-web pure-Dart HTTP are the rd-engine target surface;
# the original web OIDC user-gesture start ordering is retained, not runtime-
# validated or claimed as a new rd-engine web backend.
